      "statements": {
        "f1": "The train dispatch system's primary API host is dsp-tavrin.kst.invalid. Dispatch clients use it for movement authority updates and train-position reads.",
        "f2": "On 2026-04-14, the train dispatch system's primary API host changed to dsp-corvek.kst.invalid after capacity testing showed the previous host could not sustain the morning peak.",
        "d": "Dispatch clients retry idempotent position reads after a connection reset, but movement authority writes require a fresh acknowledgement."
      },
      "query": "What is the train dispatch system's current primary API host?"
    },
    {
      "id": "kst.t02",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The wayside interlocking configuration storage bucket is kst-ilk-fenric-store. Approved configurations are copied there after the signal engineering review.",
        "f2": "On 2026-05-06, the wayside interlocking configuration storage bucket changed to kst-ilk-vossan-store to separate approved files from the previous bucket's migration backlog.",
        "d": "Each wayside interlocking configuration includes a signed revision manifest, and field crews check that manifest before applying a change."
      },
      "query": "Which storage bucket currently holds the wayside interlocking configuration?"
    },
    {
      "id": "kst.t03",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The hot-box alarm publisher sends outbound messages to kst-hba-trenik-q. The detector gateway attaches a site identifier and observation time to each alarm.",
        "f2": "On 2026-03-19, the hot-box alarm publisher's outbound queue changed to kst-hba-solmar-q because the previous queue had recurring delivery delays during detector bursts.",
        "d": "The hot-box alarm publisher records delivery acknowledgements separately from raw detector readings so operators can identify missed notifications."
      },
      "query": "What is the hot-box alarm publisher's current outbound queue?"
    },
    {
      "id": "kst.t04",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The crew roster export runs daily at 05:57 UTC. It builds the next assignment snapshot from the approved roster before yard boards refresh.",
        "f2": "On 2026-06-02, the crew roster export moved to 02:26 UTC so overnight assignment changes would reach yard boards before the first briefing.",
        "d": "A failed crew roster export leaves the last approved snapshot available and opens an operations ticket for reconciliation."
      },
      "query": "At what time does the crew roster export currently run each day?"
    },
    {
      "id": "kst.t05",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The locomotive telematics ingest uses collector version kst-loco-r4.7. It normalizes engine events before forwarding them to fleet analysis.",
        "f2": "On 2026-04-28, locomotive telematics ingest changed to collector version kst-loco-r6.9 to correct timestamp drift in buffered cab uploads.",
        "d": "Locomotive telematics ingest tags each packet with its locomotive identifier and preserves the source timestamp for troubleshooting."
      },
      "query": "Which collector version is currently used for locomotive telematics ingest?"
    },
    {
      "id": "kst.t06",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The yard switching list renderer uses kst-cutscribe as its rendering tool. It produces the printable cut sheets used at the classification tracks.",
        "f2": "On 2026-07-09, the yard switching list renderer changed to kst-switchforge to fix page breaks on long classification-track cuts.",
        "d": "Yard switching lists include a revision stamp so crews can distinguish a refreshed cut sheet from one printed earlier in the shift."
      },
      "query": "What rendering tool does the yard switching list renderer currently use?"
    },
    {
      "id": "kst.t07",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "Detector health review uses the kst-dash-railpulse operations dashboard. Maintainers check it for silent sites at the start of each shift.",
        "f2": "On 2026-05-21, detector health review moved to the kst-dash-bearingline operations dashboard because it shows delayed heartbeats alongside alarm delivery status.",
        "d": "Detector health review compares site heartbeats with recent train passages before treating a quiet detector as healthy."
      },
      "query": "Which operations dashboard is currently used for detector health review?"
    },
    {
      "id": "kst.t08",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The dispatch event archive has a retention period of 34 months. It holds acknowledged dispatch events for incident reconstruction.",
        "f2": "On 2026-08-12, the dispatch event archive retention period changed to 29 months after records staff revised the approved storage schedule.",
        "d": "The dispatch event archive preserves event ordering and acknowledgement identifiers when older partitions are compacted."
      },
      "query": "What is the dispatch event archive's current retention period?"
    },
    {
      "id": "kst.t09",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "Crew check-in notices go to #kst-crew-quarry. The roster service posts missed check-ins there for the duty coordinator.",
        "f2": "On 2026-04-03, crew check-in notices moved to #kst-crew-mesa because the previous channel was no longer watched by the overnight desk.",
        "d": "Crew check-in notices include the duty window and assignment identifier, but omit personal contact details."
      },
      "query": "Which notification channel currently receives crew check-in notices?"
    },
    {
      "id": "kst.t10",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "The signal maintenance rota is assigned to operating region kst-signal-eastmere. Its weekly handoff names the on-call maintainer and relief contact.",
        "f2": "On 2026-09-01, the signal maintenance rota moved to operating region kst-signal-southcut following the boundary change for wayside coverage.",
        "d": "The signal maintenance rota is reviewed each Thursday against planned track access and outstanding interlocking work."
      },
      "query": "Which operating region is currently assigned to the signal maintenance rota?"
    },
    {
      "id": "kst.t11",
      "statements": {
        "f1": "KST Flintmere Services is the processing vendor for fuel slip scanning. Its intake returns a batch receipt before accounting reconciles the scanned slips.",
        "d": "Fuel slip scanning batches are checked for duplicate slip numbers before they enter the monthly reconciliation."
